{{!
    @template format_aicourse/add_section_card

    The "Add section" card that closes the AI Course section grid. It is a real <button> so it is
    keyboard reachable, and it is only rendered for a teacher with edit mode turned on. Its
    decorative plus icon carries aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"; the visible label is the
    button's accessible name.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-acf-action="add-section" - click handler in amd/src/courseformat.js; also how
      format_aicourse/local/cardcontent keeps it last in the grid.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-courseid - the course the new section is added to.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * courseid int Course ID.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courseid": 2
    }
}}
<button type="button" class="acf-card acf-card--add" data-acf-action="add-section" data-courseid="{{courseid}}">
<span class="acf-card__addicon"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 5v14"/><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
<span class="acf-card__addlabel">{{#str}} addsection, format_aicourse {{/str}}</span>
</button>
